// Package gate is the single scoped entry point for every read and write against the model: View exposes read-only queries over one workspace snapshot, translated to dto's shared vocabulary, and Tx (embedding View) adds the mutation verbs — creators, editors, deleters, refactorings — that turn the Aggregate's decisions into byte-span splices. Both are valid only for the single Engine.Read or Engine.Edit call that constructs and scopes them — never held past it. View's methods split one file per semantic category (resolvers.go, enumerators.go, scanners.go, source.go, diagnostics.go); Tx's verbs split the same way (creators.go, editors.go, refactorings.go), with pipeline.go, fragments.go, and extraction.go holding the machinery those verbs compose on.
package gate
